  <BrandBranchesGrid />

  <section class="trust-bar"><div class="wrap"><span>Licensed BHGS #A49573 · Insured</span><span>Same-day · 7 Southern California counties</span><span>$120 commercial diagnostic · waived with repair</span></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>Dexter, Iowa, ESOP, and 1894 heritage</h2>
    <p>When a Dexter Commercial unit goes down in an LA laundromat or OPL, the failures our techs at Same Day Appliance Repair run most are the vended and front-load items: a coin mechanism jam or worn slide on coin-op T-Series, a door interlock switch (heavy lid- and door-slam wear), an inverter drive fault after an LA brownout, and a drain pump clogged from customer pocket-neglect. Door gaskets on high-cycle O-Series front-loads and water-inlet valves scaled by LA hard water round out the frequent calls. We service the full Dexter line, O-Series OPL front-loads (20-80 lb), T-Series (T-350 through T-1200), T-80 stacks, Express washers, and T30/T50/T80 dryers, across the seven counties, with parts through Dexter's Fairfield Iowa-direct and authorized distributor network. Typical work runs $180-$320 for coin mechanism service, $200-$340 for a door interlock or belt or inverter reset, and $220-$380 for a water-inlet valve or door gasket. Commercial diagnostic is $120, waived with the repair, BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified (#1346255700410).</p>
    <p>Across the Dexter Commercial fleet our techs service in LA, the failures cluster in a consistent order. On coin-op T-Series, coin mechanism wear leads, jams and worn slides. Door interlock switches are next, worn by the high cycle count. Inverter-drive faults after brownouts and drain-pump clogs follow, then water-inlet valves and door gaskets on high-cycle O-Series front-loads. Drive belts and, last, belt-and-bearing service on high-cycle units round out the order. On OPL machines the programmable-controller firmware questions show up when cycles don't match the property's linen spec. Because Dexter runs simpler, mechanically-direct platforms, most of these close in a single visit with truck-stock or 1-to-3-day distributor parts.</p>
    <p>Dexter Laundry Inc. is a commercial laundry equipment manufacturer headquartered in Fairfield, Iowa. Dexter has been 100% employee-owned through an ESOP since 2004, which puts Dexter 14 years ahead of Alliance Laundry Systems (Speed Queen's parent) on the employee-ownership transition. Dexter's 1894 founding makes it among the oldest continuously operating US commercial laundry makers, alongside Huebsch (1887) and Speed Queen (1908). In operational terms, Dexter's employee-ownership shows up in the product: engineering roadmap is set by employee-owners rather than subordinated to a private-equity return horizon or a conglomerate's portfolio-integration strategy.</p>
    <p>Parts and service infrastructure: Dexter runs its own direct + authorized distributor network out of Fairfield, with regional distribution into the LA market. Parts lead times run 1-3 days on common service items through the authorized channel; common replacement parts (door gaskets, door switches, water-inlet valves, drain pumps, drive belts, pulley assemblies) are stocked on our service trucks for single-visit resolution where model compatibility matches. Dexter doesn't share a parts catalog with Alliance, Ali Group, or ITW siblings the way brands inside multi-brand conglomerates sometimes do, Dexter parts are Dexter-specific.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap">
    <h2>Dexter Commercial models we service</h2>
    <div class="model-grid">
      <div class="model-card"><h3>O-Series OPL front-loads</h3><p>O-Series 20, 30, 40, 55, 60, 80 lb capacities. Programmable OPL controller; hotel + hospital + institutional install base. Service domain: door gasket, door interlock, inverter drive, drain pump, main motor bearings, programmable controller firmware.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>T-Series laundromat washers</h3><p>T-350, T-450, T-600, T-750, T-900, T-1200 hardmount + soft-mount variants. Coin-op, card-ready, OPL-programmable configurations. Default Dexter laundromat spec. Service domain: coin mechanism, card-reader integration, door interlock, water-inlet valve, drain pump, drive belt, bearings.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>T-80 stack washer/dryer</h3><p>Stack configuration for constrained LA laundry rooms, apartment buildings, fitness centers, small OPL installs. Service spans both washer and dryer sections.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>Express high-speed washers</h3><p>Express 20, 30, 40, 60, 80 lb. High-speed cycle variants optimized for laundromat revenue-per-hour. Faster cycle times + higher extraction RPM than standard T-Series.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>T30 / T50 / T80 single-pocket dryers</h3><p>Commercial single-pocket gas or electric dryers. Gas valve, ignitor, flame sensor, burner assembly (gas); heating element (electric); blower motor, belt, door switch, lint trap sensors across both variants.</p></div>
      <div class="model-card"><h3>DL2X30 stack dryer</h3><p>Dryer-over-dryer stack configuration for laundromats + OPL. Doubled dry capacity in the same footprint; service covers both pockets with shared parts and independent gas/electric circuits.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>What breaks, inverter drives, coin mechanisms, door gaskets</h2>
    <p>Across our Dexter Commercial service volume, the failure mix overlaps substantially with Speed Queen and other Alliance-family equipment, commercial laundry mechanics are similar across manufacturers. Three domains concentrate most of the Dexter call work.</p>
    <p><b>Inverter drive faults</b> on T-Series soft-mount and O-Series front-loads follow the standard commercial laundry pattern. After LA brownout events or hard mid-cycle shutoffs, the VFD on the main motor can throw overcurrent trips on restart, drive-to-panel communication losses, or voltage-sag lockouts. Diagnostic sequence: read panel fault code, cycle the main disconnect for full drive reset, tighten the drive-to-motor output terminals, verify voltage-sag threshold settings against LA brownout conditions, test motor winding resistance. Most fault calls resolve at reset + tightening; drive replacement needed roughly 10-15% of cases.</p>
    <p><b>Coin mechanism wear</b> concentrates on T-Series coin-op variants. Coin drops jam from bent coins and accumulated grit; coin slide mechanisms wear out after several thousand cycles. Card-reader retrofit to ESD, Card Concepts, CleanCloud, or Cents is a recurring project type we coordinate with the card-system vendor. Vandalism-repair patterns depend on laundromat location and surveillance coverage.</p>
    <p><b>Door gasket replacements</b> on high-cycle O-Series and T-Series front-loads are the routine consumable. Door gaskets compress and deform over 20,000+ cycles; early signs are door-close resistance changes and small water leaks at the bottom of the door frame during spin. Replacement is a straightforward service call at $220-$380 typical.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section alt"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>What Dexter Commercial repair costs in LA</h2>
    <p>$120 flat commercial diagnostic, waived with repair.</p>
    <table class="price-table"><thead><tr><th>Repair</th><th>Typical range (parts + labor)</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Coin mechanism cleaning + realignment</td><td>$180–$320</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Door interlock switch</td><td>$200–$340</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Inverter drive fault reset + inspection</td><td>$200–$340</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Drive belt service</td><td>$200–$340</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Water-inlet valve replacement</td><td>$220–$380</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Door gasket replacement (O-Series / T-Series front-load)</td><td>$220–$380</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Coin slide replacement</td><td>$240–$420</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Drain pump replacement</td><td>$260–$440</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Programmable controller firmware reprogram</td><td>$280–$480</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Card-reader retrofit coordination (mechanical side)</td><td>$360–$640</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Main motor bearings</td><td>$380–$620</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Drum-bearing rebuild (O-Series / T-Series high-cycle)</td><td>$600–$1,000</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Control board replacement</td><td>$700–$1,200</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Inverter drive replacement</td><td>$850–$1,400</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <p class="small">Most Dexter Commercial calls land $280-$650 parts-and-labor. Inverter-drive and bearing-rebuild work runs the higher end. See <a href="/price-list/dryer-repair-cost/">commercial dryer repair cost guide</a>.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="wrap narrow">
    <h2>Dexter, related pages and alternatives</h2>
